WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.080
Welcome to this NEET Physics vector foundation supplement, using an AI

00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:06.280
generated Marin voice.

00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:11.320
Existing motion classes apply components, but we now make the vector algebra

00:00:11.320 --> 00:00:11.920
explicit.

00:00:12.740 --> 00:00:18.340
A scalar has magnitude without a spatial direction, while a vector includes a

00:00:18.340 --> 00:00:20.000
direction and follows vector addition.

00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:26.040
In a right handed Cartesian system, i hat, j hat and k hat are perpendicular

00:00:26.040 --> 00:00:28.200
unit vectors along the positive axes.

00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:34.000
Write a vector as its x component times i hat plus its y component times j hat

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:36.460
plus its z component times k hat.

00:00:37.220 --> 00:00:40.460
Its magnitude is the square root of the sum of the three squared components.

00:00:41.380 --> 00:00:45.620
A displacement three metres east and four metres north has magnitude five

00:00:45.620 --> 00:00:45.940
metres.

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:50.738
Dividing that vector by five metres gives its direction unit vector: zero

00:00:50.738 --> 00:00:51.000
point

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:53.580
six i hat plus zero point eight j hat.

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:55.980
This unit vector is dimensionless.

00:00:56.660 --> 00:01:01.480
The zero vector has zero magnitude and no unique direction, so division by its

00:01:01.480 --> 00:01:03.240
magnitude cannot define a unit vector.

00:01:03.504 --> 00:01:07.304
Vector addition combines corresponding components in a common coordinate

00:01:07.304 --> 00:01:07.724
system.

00:01:08.184 --> 00:01:13.584
For A equal to three i hat plus four j hat and B equal to minus one i hat plus

00:01:13.584 --> 00:01:17.504
two j hat, A plus B is two i hat plus six j hat.

00:01:18.144 --> 00:01:23.844
A minus B is four i hat plus two j hat, because subtracting B reverses both of

00:01:23.844 --> 00:01:24.244
its components.

00:01:24.884 --> 00:01:28.904
The magnitude of the sum is the square root of forty, not the sum of the two

00:01:28.904 --> 00:01:29.804
original magnitudes.

00:01:30.564 --> 00:01:34.684
Geometrically, placing vectors head to tail gives the same resultant as a

00:01:34.684 --> 00:01:35.724
parallelogram construction.

00:01:36.664 --> 00:01:39.544
Addition is commutative, but subtraction generally is not.

00:01:40.244 --> 00:01:45.244
To resolve a vector of magnitude A making angle theta from positive x, use A

00:01:45.244 --> 00:01:50.224
cosine theta along x and A sine theta along y, with the appropriate signs for

00:01:50.224 --> 00:01:50.764
its quadrant.

00:01:51.384 --> 00:01:55.804
If the stated angle is measured from another axis, those expressions must be

00:01:55.804 --> 00:01:56.284
interpreted accordingly.

00:01:56.284 --> 00:02:00.364
Always put both vectors in the same basis before combining their numbers.

00:02:00.624 --> 00:02:05.124
The scalar product, also called the dot product, multiplies two vector

00:02:05.124 --> 00:02:07.784
magnitudes and the cosine of their included angle.

00:02:08.684 --> 00:02:12.784
The result is a scalar, although it may be positive, negative or zero.

00:02:13.424 --> 00:02:17.960
In an orthonormal Cartesian basis, multiply matching components and add the

00:02:17.960 --> 00:02:18.444
results.

00:02:19.244 --> 00:02:24.224
For A with components two, minus one and two, and B with components one, three

00:02:24.224 --> 00:02:28.864
and zero, the dot product is two minus three plus zero, or minus one.

00:02:29.224 --> 00:02:33.544
If both vectors are nonzero, that negative sign indicates an obtuse included

00:02:33.544 --> 00:02:33.844
angle.

00:02:34.904 --> 00:02:37.564
A vector dotted with itself gives its squared magnitude.

00:02:38.524 --> 00:02:42.984
Perpendicular nonzero vectors have zero dot product, but a zero result also

00:02:42.984 --> 00:02:44.284
occurs if one vector is zero.

00:02:45.244 --> 00:02:48.104
Dot multiplication is commutative and distributive over addition.

00:02:49.224 --> 00:02:52.964
Constant force work is force dotted with displacement, so only the force

00:02:52.964 --> 00:02:54.884
component along the displacement contributes.

00:02:55.444 --> 00:02:59.724
For a ten newton force at sixty degrees to a two metre displacement, multiply

00:02:59.724 --> 00:03:01.444
ten by two by one half.

00:03:02.064 --> 00:03:03.684
The result is ten joules of work.

00:03:03.936 --> 00:03:07.653
The vector product, also called the cross product, gives a vector

00:03:07.653 --> 00:03:08.396
perpendicular

00:03:08.396 --> 00:03:12.676
to the plane of two nonparallel input vectors in three dimensional space.

00:03:13.456 --> 00:03:17.156
Its magnitude is the product of their magnitudes and the sine of the included

00:03:17.156 --> 00:03:17.536
angle.

00:03:18.576 --> 00:03:21.756
Direction follows the right hand rule in a right handed coordinate system.

00:03:22.616 --> 00:03:28.476
The cyclic relations are i hat cross j hat equals k hat, j hat cross k hat

00:03:28.476 --> 00:03:32.436
equals i hat, and k hat cross i hat equals j hat.

00:03:33.276 --> 00:03:36.096
Reversing either order changes the sign.

00:03:36.096 --> 00:03:39.936
A vector crossed with itself is zero, and the operation distributes over

00:03:39.936 --> 00:03:40.296
addition.

00:03:41.116 --> 00:03:45.876
For A equal to i hat plus two j hat and B equal to three i hat, the only

00:03:45.876 --> 00:03:50.576
nonzero term is six times j hat cross i hat, giving minus six k hat.

00:03:51.296 --> 00:03:55.376
The magnitude also gives the parallelogram area when the vectors represent

00:03:55.376 --> 00:03:55.776
sides.

00:03:55.776 --> 00:04:01.016
Torque is position crossed with force, so reversing the order reverses the

00:04:01.016 --> 00:04:03.116
direction rather than producing the same torque.
